Subject: [PATCH 0/2] media: i2c: add Samsung S5K4H8 image sensor

Hi,

This series adds a DT binding and V4L2 sub-device driver for the Samsung
S5K4H8 8 MP raw Bayer sensor (MIPI CSI-2, CCI/I2C).

Hardware:
 - Chip id 0x4088 @ 0x0000
 - 4-lane CSI-2 @ 280 MHz link (560 Mbps/lane), 24 MHz MCLK
 - Modes: 3264x2448 SGRBG10; 1632x1224 2x2 binning
 - Stream on/off: 8-bit write to 0x0100 (0x01 / 0x00)

Implementation notes:
 - Register tables adapted from the Rockchip vendor driver (GPL-2.0;
   Copyright (C) 2017 Fuzhou Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.). I/O via v4l2-cci.
 - Modern subdev active-state API (init_state, enable_streams).
 - Crop selection exposes the full pixel array; binning is 2x2 of that
   array (not a windowed crop).
 - Power sequence: supplies -> MCLK -> XSHUTDOWN deassert + settle.
 - Assisted-by: Gemini:3.6-Flash for V4L2 active-state API refactoring,
   DT schema formatting, and static analysis verification.

Non-goals for v1: board DTS, OTP/AWB, H/V flip, test pattern.

Tested on Motorola Moto E4 (perry / MSM8917) with mainline-track CAMSS
and libcamera Simple pipeline:
 - rear ~24 fps 3264x2448 SGRBG10; front OV5695 still healthy (~17.6 fps)
 - v4l2-compliance -d /dev/v4l-subdev15: Total: 46, Succeeded: 46, Failed: 0, Warnings: 0

Board DTS enablement is intentionally not included and will be a
follow-up once the binding is accepted.

Please review.

Thanks,
Aneesh

